WEBVTT

00:32:26.996 --> 00:32:31.329
I couldn't have survived in many ways
without that destructiveness

00:32:31.329 --> 00:32:37.163
and that testing of of who I was as I
revised myself, so to speak. Yeah.

00:32:37.913 --> 00:32:41.663
Do you think that part of that revision
for you was to change your name?

00:32:42.121 --> 00:32:44.788
Oh, absolutely. Mm hmm. Yeah.

00:32:45.246 --> 00:32:50.163
So I was born Cheryl Milind, as you said,
and then I got married young.

00:32:50.163 --> 00:32:53.246
I was Cheryl Milind Littig. We
we both hyphenated our names.

00:32:53.246 --> 00:32:56.454
And because we were trying to be
radical feminist and cool,

00:32:57.704 --> 00:32:59.538
which it was a weird thing
to do back then.

00:32:59.538 --> 00:33:03.996
And so, yeah, when I got divorced
right before I went to hike on